[size=6][color=#00ccff][b]AbsoluteHOTAS 5.0.0-beta[/b][/color][/size]
[size=4][b][color=#ffaa00]Native ship controls, simultaneous roll + strafe, and OpenTrack-compatible cockpit head tracking.[/color][/b][/size]

[i]This is an opt-in beta. AbsoluteHOTAS 4.0.2 remains available as the stable fallback while 5.0 receives broader hardware and ship-state testing.[/i][/center]

[line]

[center][size=5][color=#ffcc00][b]What is new in 5.0[/b][/color][/size][/center]

[list]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]Native Ship Functions:[/color][/b] All 23 named ship-button actions and named macro targets use validated internal Starfield control paths. They do not emit keyboard/mouse input or depend on the player's keybinds.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]Native Boost and Strafe:[/color][/b] The throttle boost zone and analog strafe use Starfield's internal ship-control paths. Roll and strafe remain independent and can be commanded simultaneously.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]Simultaneous Roll + Strafe:[/color][/b] Lateral and vertical strafe can both be combined with roll for full six-degree-of-freedom control.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]OpenTrack Camera Look:[/color][/b] Rotational cockpit yaw, pitch, and roll support for OpenTrack tracker sources, validated with Tobii Tracker 2 and NeuralNet webcam input.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]Camera Look Workbench:[/color][/b] Per-axis enable, inversion, sensitivity, limits, filtering, joystick overrides, toggle/recenter bindings, and live graph/readouts.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]Automatic Pilot/FPS Context:[/color][/b] Flight controls now park automatically after leaving the pilot seat. Menus/loading remain suspended rather than being mistaken for FPS, and head pose has its own conservative 400 ms safety gate.[/*]
[*][b]Fail-Closed Runtime Gates:[/b] A version or object mismatch disables the affected native operation instead of falling back to SendInput.[/*]
[/list]

[line]

[center][size=5][color=#ffaa00][b]Upgrade validation and user data[/b][/color][/size][/center]

The release archive contains only [b]AbsoluteHOTAS.dll[/b] and the mod-owned default [b]AbsoluteHOTAS.ini[/b]. It does not include or overwrite [b]AbsoluteHOTAS_Custom.ini[/b], profiles, or logs.

One real maintained 4.0.0 setup retained its bindings, profiles, and user data immediately after installing 5.0.0-beta with no rebinding. That is a successful migration smoke test, but it is still a sample of one. [b]Back up AbsoluteHOTAS_Custom.ini and the Profiles directory before installing the beta.[/b]

[line]

[center][size=5][color=#00ccff][b]Install and test[/b][/color][/size][/center]

[b]Requirements[/b]
[list]
[*]Starfield 1.16.242 or 1.16.244[/*]
[*]SFSE 0.2.20 or later[/*]
[*]OpenTrack with FreeTrack 2.0 Enhanced output only for tracker-based camera look[/*]
[*]No Starfield Address Library required[/*]
[/list]

[list=1]
[*]Back up AbsoluteHOTAS_Custom.ini and your Profiles directory.[/*]
[*]Install the archive normally with your mod manager.[/*]
[*]Launch Starfield through SFSE.[/*]
[*]Open the main or pause menu and press [color=#ffaa00][b]Ctrl+Alt+B[/b][/color].[/*]
[*]Review Flight Axes, Ship Buttons, and the new [b]Tune > Camera Look[/b] page, then Save & Apply.[/*]
[/list]

For tracker input, start OpenTrack and enable [b]freetrack 2.0 Enhanced[/b] output. Head tracking is rotational only; translation is not implemented.

[line]

[center][size=5][color=#ffcc00][b]Beta boundaries and feedback[/b][/color][/size][/center]

[b]Undock / Take-Off[/b] and [b]Exit Ship From Cockpit[/b] use native contextual routes but still need broader seated-state testing. Other devices, duplicate-device rigs, overlays, profiles, and mod stacks may reveal issues not present in the maintainer setup.

Please report reproducible crashes, configuration loss, stuck outputs, core flight regressions, failed ship actions, and tracker direction/centering issues first. Include Starfield/SFSE versions, hardware and tracker source, reproduction steps, and an AbsoluteHOTAS log with logging enabled.

[b]Rollback:[/b] reinstall the 4.0.2 DLL and default INI. Keep your backed-up AbsoluteHOTAS_Custom.ini and Profiles directory.

